      ":question/id": "17243001-2ab5-5983-a825-00b76f6856bb",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+42y-60z &=48 \\\\ 8x-56y+80z &=-64 \\\\ 4x-28y+40z &=-32\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 42 & -60 & 48 \\\\ 8 & -56 & 80 & -64 \\\\ 4 & -28 & 40 & -32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=\\left(-\\frac{1}{6}\\right)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -7 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -56 & 80 & -64 \\\\ 4 & -28 & 40 & -32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-8)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -7 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -28 & 40 & -32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -7 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"
