      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+4z &=-34 \\\\ -9x+18y-18z &=153 \\\\ -7x+14y-14z &=119\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 4 & -34 \\\\ -9 & 18 & -18 & 153 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ -9 & 18 & -18 & 153 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(7)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"
